        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c4_because_true_lid_cannot_estimated",
          "text": "Because true LID cannot be estimated at Stable Diffusion scale, the authors use three practical proxies for the model's LID: an unconditional estimate from the FLIPD algorithm, a conditional estimate, and the classifier-free guidance vector norm. They also prove that conditioning on a prompt can only reduce local dimension, explaining why specific prompts drive memorization.",
          "expected_role": "guidance",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "because",
            "true",
            "lid",
            "cannot",
            "estimated",
            "stable",
